# Context

## Background
Lands the approved background design package (task T078) plus the
per-piece in-cell designs (T95) and the zero-warning gate fix (T095).
The owner approved implementation from the imagegen concept gallery
on 2026-11-05.

## Why This Way
- Backgrounds are drawn procedurally at runtime. The PNG concept
  plates are never loaded by the game; they only set the visual
  direction.
- The concept plates and prompts are retained under tracked paths
  (docs/backgrounds, output/background-mocks) because the hosted
  gallery expires on 2026-11-08 unless claimed. New worktrees must
  not depend on that hosting.

## Gotchas
- When a plate disagrees with the renderer, the brief's limits and
  the real renderer geometry win over the image.
- Players can turn backgrounds off or pin one preferred background
  across all levels; relaunch tests cover legacy and broken
  settings files.

